WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.720 --> 00:00:06.480
So we’ve been involved in Jazz Fest since we was, like, kids you know.

2
00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:10.160
Like . . . I’ll say about six or seven.

3
00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:14.780
We went to Jazz Fest, and he used to set up long time ago out there.

4
00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:19.820
So they asked me . . . He was going to do something else,

5
00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:22.720
and they asked me did I want to do it and I was like, “Okay.”

6
00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:24.720
I actually used to work the Grandstand, too.

7
00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:36.560
But the Folks Village . . . I think it was 2007 or eight that I started doing Folks Village.

8
00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:39.200
Yeah, I don’t do the Grandstand no more, but Folks Village.

9
00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:42.580
My dad used to do it years before I did.

10
00:00:42.580 --> 00:00:50.820
So after him moving to somewhere else I was able to come in and keep the demonstration flow going with the second line culture.

11
00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:53.940
Working with the kids, like, is a Thursday.

12
00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:59.700
The second week is when all the kids from schools come in.

13
00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:04.760
It’s busy, and I love it because they’re so interested in it, and it’s not too much more.

14
00:01:04.760 --> 00:01:09.100
Like when we was going growing up in school, you know, we had . . . Well,

15
00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:14.640
we did my colors some pine cones with glitter, just something, you know.

16
00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:18.620
I don’t think it’s more of it, you know.

17
00:01:18.620 --> 00:01:25.120
And on Saturdays we used to go to the YMCA and do demonstrations of just coloring, whatever.

18
00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:27.680
But it was something interesting.

19
00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:32.720
And with the kids at Jazz Fest, once they get to my booth, it’s kind of . . . The teachers be telling them,

20
00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:34.400
“Let’s go!” and they just don’t want to move,

21
00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:41.620
you know. [laughs] That Thursday at Jazz Fest is when all the kids come, and that is the interesting part that I love.

22
00:01:41.620 --> 00:01:45.100
If I could just go set up every Thursday I’ll be alright.

23
00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:51.220
It means a whole lot because here in New Orleans it’s not much you can do.

24
00:01:51.220 --> 00:01:54.860
And single parents is the ones that’s struggling with the kids.

25
00:01:54.860 --> 00:01:57.640
I don’t look for excuses, you know, for kids.

26
00:01:57.640 --> 00:02:02.400
But it’s not there, so if it’s not there then you know they don’t have it.

27
00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:08.640
So my son, he’s seventeen now, but I try to keep him involved.

28
00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:11.420
I was a single mom raising him, you know.

29
00:02:11.420 --> 00:02:14.980
I kept him involved in a whole lot even though things I bought he would take it all loose.

30
00:02:14.980 --> 00:02:19.620
And I didn’t understand why, but it was probably part of trying to be creative.

31
00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:22.080
But it means a whole lot.

32
00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:23.820
And to see them involved in it.

33
00:02:23.820 --> 00:02:26.740
I’d like to see much more of it.
